  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "The ratio \\[\\dfrac{10^{2000}+10^{2002}}{10^{2001}+10^{2001}}\\] is closest to which of the following numbers?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0.1\\)",
    "B": "\\(0.2\\)",
    "C": "\\(1\\)",
    "D": "\\(5\\)",
    "E": "\\(10\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Each term contains the common factor \\(10^{2000}>0\\). Dividing both the numerator and denominator by it removes the large powers:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{10^{2000}+10^{2002}}{10^{2001}+10^{2001}}\n&=\\frac{1+100}{10+10}\\\\\n&=\\frac{101}{20}=5.05.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThis is only \\(0.05\\) away from \\(5\\), while every other listed choice is at least \\(4.05\\) away. The closest number is \\(\\boxed{5}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
